[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Italian Game: Giuoco Pianissimo, Quiet Fourth Moves"]
[ECO "C53"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin"]
[Themes "castle-early,solid-centre"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4.d3, 4.O-O or 4.Nc3"]
[Start "giuoco-piano 3...Bc5"]

4. d3 { Another quiet move that guards e4. } ( 4. O-O Nf6 5. d3 d6 ) ( 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. d3 d6 6. Bg5 h6 { Asks the bishop what it wants: if it takes on f6, Black recaptures with the queen. } 7. Bxf6 ( 7. Bh4 a6 { Gives the bishop on c5 a safe square on a7, and keeps Black ready for ...g5 if the pin on f6 becomes a nuisance. } ) 7... Qxf6 8. Nd5 Qd8 ) ( 4. d4 { Opens the centre at once. After ...exd4 it is the Scotch Gambit position: Black meets 5.c3 with ...Nf6, 5.O-O with ...d6 and 5.Ng5 with ...Nh6. } 4... exd4 ) 4... Nf6 { Attacks e4 and develops. Black plays the same plan against every quiet fourth move. } 5. O-O d6 { Supports e5 and frees the c8 bishop. } 6. c3 { This transposes into the main line, the Giuoco Pianissimo. } ( 6. h3 a6 { The same plan as always: ...a6 gives the bishop the a7 square, then ...O-O and ...h6. } ) ( 6. Bg5 h6 { Asks the bishop to take on f6 or retreat. After Bxf6 Qxf6, Black has the two bishops. } ) ( 6. Nc3 a6 ) 6... O-O *
